<!--
  This file records the ApiCompat breaks in Azure.ResourceManager.ProviderHub 1.3.0 that are NOT
  caused by the upstream compliance change to the Microsoft.ProviderHub specification.

  Everything below comes from regenerating the package on the current management-plane generator:
  a model that was promoted to an ARM resource, an operation that gained a WaitUntil parameter, an
  enum that was renamed and widened, and a property that was un-flattened. These are recoverable
  through client.tsp customizations or retained custom code, so they are recorded individually to
  keep them reviewable rather than folded into the compliance removals.

  The compliance-driven removals are deliberately NOT listed here. ApiCompat suppression targets are
  fully qualified signatures, so recording them would reproduce in this repository the internal-only
  Microsoft identifiers that the upstream change exists to remove. They are described by location and
  shape in the package CHANGELOG.md instead.

  NOTE: this file is currently not consumed by the build. ApiCompat is gated on a non-empty
  <ApiCompatVersion> in the project file (see eng/Directory.Build.Common.targets), which is absent
  for this package, and Azure.ResourceManager.ProviderHub is listed in ApiCompatVersionOptOut.txt.
  The entries below are therefore a record for reviewers, not active suppressions. If ApiCompat is
  re-enabled for this package, this file will need the compliance removals added as well or the
  build will fail on them.
-->
